# tools/g/glow_choir_witness.rish -- the Glow witnesses no other runner reached.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/g/glow_choir_witness.rish
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. On 20260828 a survey asked which Glow-family witnesses any runner on disk
# actually names, and 26 answered nobody: not the standing roster, not the three tend suites,
# not another witness. They had been proving nothing since the day each landed. Run by hand that
# morning, 25 stood GREEN and one was RED -- tools/g/glow_g5_nock_family_notes_witness.rish
# cited active-designing/20260720-033200_stoa98-g5-nock-second-backend-family-notes.md, a brief
# that folded to active-designing/yonder/date/20260720/ and left the assert reading a missing
# file rather than a Nock fact. A witness nobody runs cannot report the day it breaks.
#
# WHAT IT PROVES. Every path below exists on disk, and then every one of them runs GREEN. A RED
# names exactly which member broke. Membership is a plain list rather than a discovered set, so
# a reader can see the whole roster without running anything.
#
# WHAT IT DOES NOT PROVE, AND WHO DOES. Completeness -- whether a Glow witness landing tomorrow
# is reached by anything -- belongs to tools/w/witness_reach_witness.rish, whose `unreached`
# ratchet falls by exactly the count this choir carries. A second bijection here would be a
# second loom watching one lantern, so this file registers and runs, and the ratchet counts.
#
# COST, MEASURED 20260828 ON THIS PIER. 2m01s for all 26: the members are grep-shaped and cheap, save
# active-designing/docs/glow/glow_book_anchor_witness.rish at 25s. That is a cadence clock rather
# than a lap one -- the roster's own rule, cost decides the tier.
#
# THE SECOND SURVEY, 20260909, AND WHY THE POPULATION REFILLED. `sh
# tools/fixtures/w/witness_reach_scan.sh --list` reads the `unheard` band -- a tracked
# `*_witness.rish` no runner on disk names in command position -- and it answered eight Glow-family
# files, none of them among the 26 above. Run one at a time before any was gathered, all eight
# stood GREEN. Six join the choir here: glow_connector_seam (1s), glow_jamcue_vectors (0s),
# glow_repl (78s), glow_skate_gates (61s), nock_glow_mirror (17s) and stoa71_glow_import_seam (6s),
# so the choir's members go 26 -> 32 and its cost 2m01s -> 4m47s measured on this pier, still choir
# money on the cadence clock.
#
# TWO OF THE EIGHT ARE HELD, AND THE HOLD IS THE POINT. glow_mobile_target and glow_riscv_target
# each read GREEN in 0s on this host by SKIPPING: `qemu-aarch64 is absent`, `qemu-riscv64 is
# absent`. Whether that is an honest green or a green that means nothing is REDS `%460`, OPEN and
# Keaton's word, with `%446` reading the other way. Gathering them would publish a fleet-wide
# green for a leg no ship on this pier runs, which is the proxy shape REDS `%532` booked one room
# over. They wait for the ruling rather than for a lap.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT REACH, MEASURED THE SAME HOUR. 57 further Glow witnesses read `unclocked`
# rather than `unheard`: `tools/p/parity_ch01.rish` names every one of them, and no roster row
# reaches parity_ch01. A second choir over that list would be a second loom watching one lantern,
# which this file's own paragraph above forbids. The answer there is a tier for the parity runner,
# it costs build time, and witness_reach_scan.sh's own header already names it as Keaton's word.

say "glow-choir: Language EN -- the Glow witnesses no other runner named."
say "glow-choir: Style Gauge, Meter -- a RED names the member that broke."
say "glow-choir: Lens TAME -- every member asserted present before any is run; the choir stops loud on the first red."

